{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470553-subdermal-armor-implants","id":1470553,"title":"Subdermal armor / implants","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-12-15T14:26:11-08:00","id":1470553,"title":"Subdermal armor / implants","content":"I was thinking...<br /> <br /> since the undead:<br /> <br /> - do not get tired, so they can carry some extra weight for hours without incurring exaustion<br /> - have no problems like infections / tissue reject / inflamations<br /> - have not the problem of blood acting as corrosive for implants<br /> <br /> then why not getting subdermal armor and reinforcing in the bones? Beside protection and increased brawl damage, that could even provide some protection from fire and sunlight ( aramid fabric , kevlar, teflon ecc. ), even if the outer layer of skin would still be lost at least the damage would not go deeper.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","name":"Solomon Draak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-15T16:04:31-08:00","id":1470557,"title":"","content":"Vampire bodies do reject modifications though, so that's probably a big reason (even if there are ways around that).<br /> <br /> Traditionally, this has been the purview of Vicissitude to handle as ideas for mechanics.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-15T18:23:59-08:00","id":1470571,"title":"","content":"i imagine that their ability to regenerate would simply end up pushing the implants out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>they/them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27123-littlewitchmaus","name":"littlewitchmaus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-15T20:11:58-08:00","id":1470580,"title":"","content":"Yeah, if I recall implants (even those put into a vampire back when they were still mortal) will eventually be pushed out of the body as they naturally regenerate. So someone who had metal pins put into a broken leg bone 20 years before they became a vampire will wake up one night in their coffin to see the pins jutting out of their skin. This would apply to any other implants put into the vampire after they've become one of the undead. Vicissitude alterations are permanent (though a vampire can heal those as Aggravated damage) so if the implants were used in conjunction with Vicissitude they could be permanent. I would expect such things to be much more common among the Sabbat than elsewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-15T22:54:34-08:00","id":1470585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470553-subdermal-armor-implants?p=1470580#post1470580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, if I recall implants (even those put into a vampire back when they were still mortal) will eventually be pushed out of the body as they naturally regenerate.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is false. The Vampire retains everything they had when they were embraced, it's a permanent part of them. Tattoos for instance will re-ink themselves no matter how many times the flesh they're on is torn out and mended. So fake tits, a hip implant, or a quick nip-tuck is all very eternal and you can continually remove and regenerate titanium hips till the end of your unlife (it's very likely that such things will have altered properties and won't be &quot;real&quot; titanium hips, kinda like how things conjured by the path of conjuring are imitations) <br /> <br /> Adressing the OP's question<br /> Yeah you could probably do subdermal implants (if you had vicissitude) but I don't think they're going to be very practical as they're going to compromise movement and appearance. External armour is just better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-16T02:17:39-08:00","id":1470591,"title":"","content":"Subdermal implants also just feel very counter to Vampires internal setting; in a broader WoD where it\u2019s a Mage crossover they\u2019d make some sense, but would also be heavily skewing towards the hypertech of Mage and the feel of that line where vampires are just one common type of supernatural critter in a see of bygones and thaumivores that might be augmented by technomagick.<br /> <br /> By contrast, Vampire on its own skews more \u201cdarker version of the real world\u201d when it comes to the sort of tech is around and the sort of creatures that go bump in the night; vampires, ghouls, revenants, dhampirs, with crossover elements of savage werewolves (which aren\u2019t quite the Garou unless you wanna run it as a crossover), ghosts aplenty, mystic sorcerers (magic as presented in VtM is more linear than Mage\u2019s spheres) and the occasional demon. The best tech out there is the best tech out here\u2026 which is still damned useful if you\u2019re hunting the damned, but isn\u2019t in the tealm of sci-fi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-16T03:09:49-08:00","id":1470595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470553-subdermal-armor-implants?p=1470585#post1470585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is false. The Vampire retains everything they had when they were embraced, it's a permanent part of them. Tattoos for instance will re-ink themselves no matter how many times the flesh they're on is torn out and mended. So fake tits, a hip implant, or a quick nip-tuck is all very eternal and you can continually remove and regenerate titanium hips till the end of your unlife (it's very likely that such things will have altered properties and won't be &quot;real&quot; titanium hips, kinda like how things conjured by the path of conjuring are imitations)</div> </div> </div> </div>Any chance you could tell me which book says that vampires regenerate stuff like titanium hips. I was familiar with the idea, and I've found material that says, that tattoos applied before the embrace are permanent, whilst for those created after the embrace, the ink is pushed out before the vampire rises the next night (Guide to the Camarilla, p200). And I do recall reading something somewhere about tattoos reappearing even if the limb is cut off and regrown, but I can't find it in any of the pdfs I've got.<br /> <br /> I would have consider tattoos reappearing as fairly innocuous - but other implants 'regrowing' seems a bit far fetched. A canny vampire (but callous) could embace someone with a titanium hip - or some other precious metal implant - and simply cut if off/out before dawn - to have a neverending supply. That doesn't seem to me to be within the spirit of the vampire regenerating its physical form each night (although well aware I may be wrong). Without a booksource indicating otherwise, I'd be more inclined to say that the shape of the bone regenerates as if the titanium hip would be there - but the titanium itself would not be. Which would presumbly be very unpleasant for the vampire who was now missing an implant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":699,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/699-malleusxxiii","user":"MalleusXXIII","date":". 12-16-2021, 06:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/699-malleusxxiii","name":"MalleusXXIII","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar699_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-16T03:10:47-08:00","id":1470596,"title":"","content":"I like Hypertech across all the WoD be it Vampire, Mage or Werewolf. Obscenely wealthy elites having access to all kinds of technologies too good or dangerous for the unwashed masses to get their grubby hands on? love it. It shouldn't be centre stage with vampire like it is with Mage and anything weaver centric, but it is very good when used to accentuate disparity in vampire. <br /> <br /> <br /> But, uh... external armour is really good, and A lot of the issues with external armour (comfort, breathability, weight*) aren't problems for vampires at all. Vampires would have a much better time doing a Ned Kelly than they would a... Adam Jensen? A vampire can easily get armour that looks like ordinary clothing, and a vampire with Potence can easily wear a thick suit of steel. Subdermal stuff just sounds really difficult, really complicated, really expensive, and not really worth it when Vampires have disciplines. Also I think Subdermal armour would complicate wounds a lot; remember that a vampire can have a gunshot go straight through them and suffer little. Things unpleasant and messy when the gunshot doesn't go straight through them but instead the impact is distributed over an area of their internals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-16T03:32:39-08:00","id":1470599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MalleusXXIII</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470553-subdermal-armor-implants?p=1470595#post1470595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Any chance you could tell me which book says that vampires regenerate stuff like titanium hips.<br /> <br /> A canny vampire (but callous) could embace someone with a titanium hip - or some other precious metal implant - and simply cut if off/out before dawn - to have a neverending supply. That doesn't seem to me to be within the spirit of the vampire regenerating its physical form each night (although well aware I may be wrong). Without a booksource indicating otherwise, I'd be more inclined to say that the shape of the bone regenerates as if the titanium hip would be there - but the titanium itself would not be. Which would presumbly be very unpleasant for the vampire who was now missing an implant.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I was just extrapolating from the Tattoos. Titanium is quite special in that it's very non-reactive, so maybe it never really mystically bonds with the body enough to regenerate. Maybe the vampire really needs to make sure the hip stays in, otherwise they've just got a hollow area that needs a replacement part inserted. Still, A titanium bone is the most extreme example; putting it back into the body after a gruesome battle might be an interesting activity, but things quickly become rediculous when you're constantly looking for fresh silicon to shove into your chest because your fake tits took a nasty hit in the last fight.<br /> <br /> (side note and I kinda got this from reading things wrong but anyhow: Regrowing something that was missing is explicitly NOT a priveledge the embrace allows. An injury you got just before the embrace? Sure. Something you've had for long enough that a replacement occurred. No. You are not going to get a nice calcium bone to replace your titanium hip.)<br /> <br /> <br /> Actively exploiting how you've got infinite Titanium hips is... well... stupid. A golden hip isn't much better. Most vampires can get rich without something so conspicuous as selling off golden bones.<br /> 1-It's a great way for thaumaturges to target you. That hip is a part of you, and it won't degrade easy. Holding a part of you is a good way to make a spell targeting you easier.<br /> 2-There are very likely other mystical issues with the hip, given that it was grown magically by a vampire's regeneration. Perhaps it's weak to sunlight, perhaps it can't change state like thaumaturgical constructions. A golden bone you can't melt down isn't something you can get rich off.<br /> 3- How many fucking uses do you think all those titanium hips have? Are you going to become disgustingly rich from selling hips? Are titanium hips a deadly secret weapon? Is this a power greater than a discipline or path? No, not really.<br /> <br /> Put it another way, are werewolves donating their ever regenerating bodies to solving world hunger or at least to make a really profitable and possibly ethical butchery? No. There's consequences for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 12-16-2021, 10:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-16T03:41:10-08:00","id":1470601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470553-subdermal-armor-implants?p=1470599#post1470599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was just extrapolating from the Tattoos (and your idea is bad, I'll get back to that in a bit). Titanium is quite special in that it's very non-reactive, so maybe it never really mystically bonds with the body enough to regenerate. Maybe the vampire really needs to make sure the hip stays in, otherwise they've just got a hollow area that needs a replacement part inserted. Still, A titanium bone is the most extreme example; putting it back into the body after a gruesome battle might be an interesting activity, but things quickly become rediculous when you're constantly looking for fresh silicon to shove into your chest because your fake tits took a nasty hit in the last fight.<br /> <br /> Regrowing something that was missing is explicitly NOT a priveledge the embrace allows. An injury you got just before the embrace? Sure. Something you've had for long enough that a replacement occured. No. You are not going to get a nice calcium bone to replace your titanium hip.<br /> <br /> <br /> Actively exploiting how you've got infinite Titanium hips is... well... stupid. A golden hip isn't much better. Most vampires can get rich without something so conspicuous as selling off golden bones.<br /> 1-It's a great way for thaumaturges to target you. That hip is a part of you, and it won't degrade easy. Holding a part of you is a good way to make a spell targetting you easier.<br /> 2-There are very likely other mystical issues with the hip, given that it was grown magically by a vampire's regeneration. Perhaps it's weak to sunlight, perhaps it can't change state like thaumaturgical constructions.<br /> 3- How many fucking uses do you think all those titanium hips have? Are you going to become disgustingly rich from selling hips? Are titanium hips a deadly secret weapon? Is this a power greater than a discipline or path? No, not really.<br /> <br /> Put it another way, are werewolves donating their ever regenerating bodies to solving world hunger or at least to make a really profitable and possibly ethical butchery? No. There's consequences for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the feedback on my comment.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/699-malleusxxiii","name":"MalleusXXIII","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar699_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-16T06:48:41-08:00","id":1470621,"title":"","content":"I agree with most of what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a> said here.<br /> <br /> First of all, bluntly put, Vampire has a real problem with a general lack of support rules for equipment and stuff outside their direct powers and bloodlines. This isn't thematic, this is silly, because it only makes their world less fleshed out. We are told about all sorts of things that exist and can be explored, yet we have no rules for them.<br /> <br /> Vampires with implants and whatnot, sci-fi or not, is just a flavor of body horror. Why can we have a Vozhd, but not someone with metal bolts jolting out of their flesh?<br /> <br /> On the regenerating materials... if tattoos can re-ink then anything goes. Seriously, ink is already just as alien to the body as metals, if it can come back mystically then why not titanium? To begin with, titanium isn't the \u00fcber metal some people think, it is just lighter steel and not that much costlier, it is used i aviation and spacecrafts because it is light, not &quot;strong&quot; (it is the strongest you get with something half the density of iron).<br /> <br /> How to stop it from getting silly? Well, send the regrown bits to the same place other vampire body parts go after being cut. Maybe it just decays rapidly into dust, because it isn't real metal, but a mystic simulacrum. Maybe the original is the thing that vanishes as the Curse claims back from the world anything that belongs to the vampire's &quot;original&quot; body. Either way, the only effect is that a character without a flaw to represent the absence of an implant have a guarantee to go back to their original shape and sheet when regenerating. Which is the intended effect anyway.<br /> <br /> And I'm all in for more <i><u>possibilities</u></i> of sci-fi and magic in the setting, something beyond the vampires themselves. The most we have as actual rules now are scarce statistics on blades made with very specific elder level powers. <b>That</b> is silly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}